# {{ name }} MI v1

{{ description }}

The business logic is in **src/main/java/com/solace/mi/Core.java**. Application.java is the standard transport. The project uses the Solace MDK 4.3.11 dependency platform with Spring Cloud Stream and Java 17; it does not load the stock connector workflow engine.

## Start a local demo

Install Docker with Compose, unzip this directory, then run:

```bash
./scripts/install.sh --demo
./scripts/smoke.sh --demo
```

Docker builds and runs the MI and a local broker; host Java and Maven are optional. The smoke test publishes a uniquely correlated input message and checks the exact output bytes from the running MI. Inspect health at http://localhost:18080/actuator/health and logs with `docker compose logs integration`.

To stop the demo: `docker compose -f compose.yaml -f compose.demo.yaml down`. Demo broker credentials are default/default and management is admin/admin; the demo broker is not exposed on host ports.

